{"title":"2004 IMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Problems of the 45th <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO\">IMO</a> 2004 Athens, Greece.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Resources\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Resources</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be an acute-angled triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/d/e5d9ab1115f581d4e52ad1477e8098917ce3745d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB\\neq AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"18\" />. The circle with diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> intersects the sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. Denote by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> the midpoint of the side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. The bisectors of the angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/5862947b38a495ec9be80e5b9c7582de6cf0d269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/4/1144897a4151dfb35088ff95aa3a3c430bbe7886.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle MON$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" /> intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Prove that the circumcircles of the triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ee98ebc2ee8d41487b27bd92258b8fa739cb84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BMR$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/8/7e8674183d1e14cf328cfede641468c412a70af9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CNR$\" width=\"45\" height=\"12\" /> have a common point lying on the side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2004 IMO Problems/Problem 1\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find all polynomials <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> with real coefficients such that for all reals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/3/123bf434194420af32656c7d781a101c96db2254.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab + bc + ca = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"127\" height=\"14\" /> we have the following relations\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/c/ffc10b907c24b5bb71310bf84a608863d9abdcc3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(a - b) + f(b - c) + f(c - a) = 2f(a + b + c).\\]\" width=\"368\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2004 IMO Problems/Problem 2\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Define a \"hook\" to be a figure made up of six unit squares as shown below in the picture, or any of the figures obtained by applying rotations and reflections to this figure.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/4/ef4cdb21baa20a696547d85c9c5773637ad93506.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.5 cm);  draw((0,0)--(1,0)); draw((0,1)--(1,1)); draw((2,1)--(3,1)); draw((0,2)--(3,2)); draw((0,3)--(3,3)); draw((0,0)--(0,3)); draw((1,0)--(1,3)); draw((2,1)--(2,3)); draw((3,1)--(3,3)); [/asy]\" width=\"75\" height=\"75\" />\n</p><p>Determine all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/5/dc5c773a00becebf2fe78e775d5953e138efea9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\times n$\" width=\"48\" height=\"9\" /> rectangles that can be covered without gaps and without overlaps with hooks such that;\n(a) the rectangle is covered without gaps and without overlaps,\n(b) no part of a hook covers area outside the rectangle.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2004 IMO Problems/Problem 3\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/e/49e6a2d706867d6652d7edadccc3fd034130bd98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> be an integer. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/7/6e761ce77e041965e1931e7387b9b140e7828832.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_1, t_2, \\dots ,t_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" /> be positive real numbers such that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/6/ba65423b7f49161183ab65b702bf0dadb017ee63.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n^2 + 1 &gt; \\left( t_1 + t_2 + ... + t_n \\right) \\left( \\frac {1}{t_1} + \\frac {1}{t_2} + ... + \\frac {1}{t_n} \\right).\\]\" width=\"386\" height=\"43\" />\nShow that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/3/273e0046b505d99f3d1167caa82b2ac76c96d075.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/5/a652022db81b0ec1c066b09e32932b7b7e0cd716.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"15\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/f/5df9ff73586b830a77fd20e48c09ec0621c07db8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> are side lengths of a triangle for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/5/ab58307d8a20377d430885cf4d2c2c342e910abf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\leq i &lt; j &lt; k \\leq n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2004 IMO Problems/Problem 4\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>In a convex quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, the diagonal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> bisects neither the angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> nor the angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/c/17ccf9ac51faa912a5338f4ebde95b5d3a0f7fb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CDA$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />. The point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies inside <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> and satisfies<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/7/977f696cf8654292a2d57df388ce9a1baff926af.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle PBC = \\angle DBA \\text{ and } \\angle PDC = \\angle BDA.\\]\" width=\"315\" height=\"13\" />\nProve that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a cyclic quadrilateral if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/5/d854fcbb426e0d95c5e3b03c2ff72cffcd2bd61a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP = CP.$\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2004 IMO Problems/Problem 5\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We call a positive integer alternating if every two consecutive digits in its decimal representation have a different parity.\n</p><p>Find all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> has a multiple which is alternating.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2004 IMO Problems/Problem 6\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO\" title=\"2004 IMO\">2004 IMO</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3831_2004_imo\">IMO 2004 Problems on the Resources page</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO\" title=\"2004 IMO\">2004 IMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2003 IMO Problems\">2003 IMO Problems</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2004 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2004 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2004 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2004 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2004 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2004 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2005 IMO Problems\">2005 IMO Problems</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018050331\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.030 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.046 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 265/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 854/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 74/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7514/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.540      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.540      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:20877:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018050331 and revision id 147633. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}